# Contact form.
#
# The form posts to /api/kontakt. Without the two required variables the route
# answers 503, and the form tells the visitor it cannot send and hands them the
# finished message to copy or open in their own mail app — no enquiry is lost,
# but none of them reach an inbox automatically either. Set these in the Vercel
# project settings before the site takes traffic.

# Required. An API key from resend.com.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Required. A verified sender on a domain you own, e.g. "Kestro <noreply@kestro.dk>".
CONTACT_FROM=
# Optional. Where enquiries land. Defaults to company.email in lib/company.ts.
CONTACT_TO=

# Optional. Every enquiry is also posted as JSON here — a CRM inbound hook
# (HubSpot, Pipedrive), an automation (Make, Zapier), or a sheet. Failures are
# logged and ignored; the email is the source of truth.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Optional. Sent as "Authorization: Bearer …" with the webhook.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# Search engine ownership.
#
# Not secrets — a verification token is a public claim of ownership and is
# visible in the page source of every verified site. They are variables
# because they differ per property, so verifying is a setting and a redeploy
# rather than a commit.
#
# Without a verified property there is no record of a single search
# impression, click, position or crawl error anywhere: Google keeps that data
# and only shows it to the verified owner. DNS verification is the better
# route where the domain's records are reachable — this is the fallback that
# works from the site itself.

# Optional. The content of the google-site-verification tag from Search Console.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# Optional. The content of the msvalidate.01 tag from Bing Webmaster Tools.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# Instagram comment replies.
#
# The webhook at /api/instagram/webhook answers praise automatically and
# forwards everything else — questions, complaints, anything the classifier is
# unsure about — to CONTACT_TO for a person. See lib/instagram.ts for what
# counts as praise; it is deliberately narrow.
#
# Without IG_APP_SECRET and IG_ACCESS_TOKEN the route answers 503 and nothing
# is sent. Setting only IG_VERIFY_TOKEN is enough to complete Meta's
# subscription handshake, so the webhook can be wired up and verified before
# any reply is ever posted.
#
# Setup, in order:
#   1. kestro.dk must be an Instagram Professional account (Business/Creator).
#   2. Create an app at developers.facebook.com and connect the account.
#   3. Ask for instagram_basic and instagram_manage_comments.
#   4. Subscribe the webhook to the "comments" field, pointing at
#      https://www.kestro.dk/api/instagram/webhook with the verify token below.
#   5. Generate a long-lived access token.

# Required to accept a payload at all. Meta signs every delivery with it, and
# an unsigned or wrongly signed request is refused — without this anyone who
# learns the URL can post fake comment events.
IG_APP_SECRET=
# Required to post replies. A long-lived token from the app above.
IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Any random string. You type the same one into Meta's webhook form; it is only
# used for the one-time subscription handshake.
IG_VERIFY_TOKEN=
# Optional but recommended. The account's own Instagram user id, so a comment
# posted by the brand itself is never answered by the brand.
IG_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Optional. Instagram Login accounts use graph.instagram.com; an account linked
# through a Facebook Page uses graph.facebook.com. Defaults to the former.
IG_GRAPH_BASE=

# Admin panel (/admin).
#
# The panel lists the enquiries the contact forms received, lets you answer
# them without opening a mail client, and shows the site's own visit counts.
# Nothing about it is required: with none of these set, the forms still email
# as they always did and /admin shows a locked screen.

# Required to open the panel at all. Without it /admin is closed to everyone,
# which is the right way for a missing variable to fail.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Optional. Signs the session cookie. Set it to any long random string and
# changing the password no longer logs you out — and logging every session out
# no longer means changing the password. Falls back to ADMIN_PASSWORD.
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# Storage, for the enquiry archive and the visit counts.
#
# Create a Neon database under Storage in the Vercel dashboard and connect it
# to the project; Vercel sets DATABASE_URL itself and the tables are created on
# first use. Without it the panel says so plainly and the rest of the site is
# unaffected — an enquiry that reaches the inbox but not the archive is a
# missing feature, not a lost customer.
DATABASE_URL=
